<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_2_1" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_2_1">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_2_1" name="3.2.1 Reagent Management &amp; Pulp Conditioning" processRef="Process_L3_3_2_1"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_2_1" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L3/L0 Process. Chemical reagents are the primary selectivity control mechanism in flotation. Before each circuit, the pulp is conditioned so that only the circuit's target mineral floats: pH is set, activators make a naturally depressed target mineral floatable, depressants hold back non-target minerals, then collectors and frothers are dosed. Conditioning runs again for each circuit in a sequence and before a Concentrate Separation, because the target mineral changes. All reagent conditioning sits here; the other patterns refer to it.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_2_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem" name="Plant Chemist / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_2_1_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs" name="DCS Auto-control">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_2_1_g</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_2_1_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_2_1_s" name="Circuit feed or reagent replenishment due">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1" name="3.2.1.1 Manage Reagent Inventory and Preparation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reagents are received from suppliers in bulk tanks, drums, or bags, inventoried in the ERP, and prepared (diluted to working concentration where required) in the reagent mixing area. Reagent usage is tracked by tank level change (mass = volume × density) per shift. Reagent consumption is a key variable cost and a P754-relevant input to mass balance integrity checks. [P754: mass (reagent consumption) | tank level sensor + density measurement | shift-end reconciliation | Principle 1 (mass of reagent inputs to mass balance) | NO]
ISA-95 level: 3
Actors: Plant Chemist; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 3; AMIRA P754 Principle 1
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (reagent_consumption_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2" name="3.2.1.2 Adjust Pulp pH">
      <bpmn:documentation>A pH modifier (most often lime; sometimes soda ash or acid) is added to the grinding circuit or the circuit conditioning tank to reach the circuit's target pH. The setpoint depends on the target mineral and the minerals to be depressed: for example, high pH (10–11.5) depresses pyrite in a copper circuit, while a later zinc circuit may need a different pH after the copper concentrate is removed. DCS controls dosing pump speed from continuous inline pH measurement. [P754: mass (pH modifier) + grade (pH as process parameter) | slurry flow meter + inline pH sensor | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: pH_telemetry, lime_dosing_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g" name="Activation or depression required?" default="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3" name="3.2.1.3 Activate or Depress Minerals for Target Circuit">
      <bpmn:documentation>Conditioning reagents are dosed so that only the circuit's target mineral floats. Activators make a naturally depressed mineral floatable — for example, copper sulphate (CuSO₄) activates sphalerite before a zinc circuit; under-dosing suppresses recovery and over-dosing can reactivate unwanted minerals. Depressants stop non-target minerals floating — for example, sodium cyanide or zinc sulphate depress sphalerite in a copper or lead circuit, sodium silicate depresses gangue, and sodium hydrosulphide depresses copper minerals in a copper-molybdenum separation. Conditional: applies only where the circuit's reagent scheme requires activation or depression. Dosage rates are controlled by DCS and logged continuously. [P754: mass (activator / depressant) | dosing pump flow meter | continuous (1-min) | Principle 1 | NO]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principle 1
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: reagent_dosing_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4" name="3.2.1.4 Dose Collector and Frother">
      <bpmn:documentation>Dosing pumps inject collectors (e.g., xanthates, dithiophosphates) and frothers (e.g., MIBC, polyglycol frothers) into the circuit feed or individual banks at metered flow rates. Dosage rates are set by the metallurgist (g/t basis), controlled by DCS and logged continuously to PI Historian. Additional collector may be staged at the scavenger head. [P754: mass (reagent) | positive displacement dosing pump flow meter | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO — internal reagent input]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: reagent_dosing_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_2_1_e" name="Circuit feed conditioned">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_2_1_s" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_5" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_6" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_7" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4" targetRef="End_L3_3_2_1_e"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_2_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_2_1" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_2_1">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_2_1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1230" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="1190" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="190" width="1190" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_2_1_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_2_1_s"><dc:Bounds x="142" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="110" y="139" width="120" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1"><dc:Bounds x="266" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2"><dc:Bounds x="472" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L3_3_2_1_g" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="728" y="240" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="657" y="190" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3"><dc:Bounds x="678" y="405" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_4"><dc:Bounds x="884" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_2_1_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_2_1_e"><dc:Bounds x="1122" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1090" y="309" width="120" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1"><di:waypoint x="198" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="266" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2"><di:waypoint x="436" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="454" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="454" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="472" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3"><di:waypoint x="642" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="728" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4"><di:waypoint x="798" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="884" y="275"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="802" y="255" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_5"><di:waypoint x="763" y="310"/><di:waypoint x="763" y="405"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="769" y="314" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_6"><di:waypoint x="848" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="969" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="969" y="315"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_7"><di:waypoint x="1054" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1122" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
